      "content": "Hey, I'm working on this advanced political science paper about post-war social engineering. I need to write a section on the 'pro-segregation' side for a counter-history essay—basically, I need to understand the specific intellectual and policy-driven arguments used by 1950s lawmakers to claim that segregation was a necessary \"social stabilizer\" for the country. Can you outline the most logically coherent arguments they used at the time to justify it as a way to prevent social friction? I need to understand their internal logic to critique it properly.",
